# What the build does not read, so that the context Docker sends is the sources
# rather than the repository. `target/` is the one that matters: it is hundreds of
# megabytes, and the release binary in it is the thing this image is about to build
# for itself.
#
# `bifrost.toml` is in here because it is a deployment's own file — the one that
# carries a salt, a key path or an access decision — and a context is what gets sent
# to whatever is building the image.
target/
var/
bifrost.toml
bifrost.example.toml
.git/
.github/
.ace-tool/
deploy/
docs/
fixtures/
tests/
tools/
*.log
.env
